title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf metarecord
catalog: CLI command
target: mf metarecord
summary: Metarecord operations: `mf metarecord [selector] <verb>`

!! Reference

```
Metarecord operations: `mf metarecord [selector] <verb>`

The selector picks the target metarecord(s) and precedes the verb:
`-q "<DSL query>"` (add `-s` for the simplified language), `-i <uuid>`
for a single metarecord, or none to mean all. Examples:
  mf metarecord get                         # every uuid
  mf metarecord -i <uuid> get               # one metarecord, full JSON
  mf metarecord -q 'rating > 3' get         # matching uuids
  mf metarecord -q 'mfr_path ->* "/docs"' field set reviewed:bool=true

Usage: mf metarecord [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  get     Read: -i <uuid> → full JSON; -q/none → UUIDs (--select for fields)
  add     Create a metarecord with the given fields and print its UUID (no selector)
  set     Replace the ENTIRE field set of the selected metarecord (needs -i, force)
  delete  Delete the selected metarecords (metadata and all fields)
  field   Field operations scoped to the selected metarecord(s)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -q, --query <QUERY>
          DSL query selector (use -s to write it in the simplified language)

  -i, --id <ID>
          Single-metarecord selector by UUID

      --eq <EQ>
          Exact-match selector: name[:type]=value (repeatable, AND-ed; safe — no DSL interpolation). Mutually exclusive with -q/-i

  -s, --simplified
          Treat -q as simplified-language text and expand it first

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
```
